 "exercise": {
  "id": "pqp03-ex08",
  "chapter": 3,
  "number": "3.8",
  "title": "Dirac notation on one line",
  "level": 2,
  "statement": "For each of the diagrams **A**, **B** and **C**, write a Dirac expression in the Dirac Formula Editor (choose the diagram in its menu) and press **Verify**. Write your own before you look at Generate.\n\n- **A** is a state, a box and an effect: the box is the X gate, with matrix $\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$.\n- **B** has two outputs. Write it twice: once with $\\otimes$, and once with the kets side by side, $|a\\rangle|b\\rangle$ or $|ab\\rangle$.\n- **C** has an effect on only one of two wires: you will need an identity, $I$, on the other.",
  "done": "Verify shows ✓ Equivalent for A, for both forms of B, and for C.",
  "book": "textbook/ch03.html#ex-3-8"
 }
